    "extractionWarnings": null,
    "metadata": "{\"summary\":\"Artificial intelligence regulation refers to the policies, laws, and guidelines governments and organizations create to oversee the development, deployment, and use of AI technologies. Recent years have seen significant regulatory activity, especially in regions like the European Union and some U.S. states, with efforts focusing on transparency, safety, and ethical AI use.rstreet+3​Global Regulation Approaches\\n\\nThe European Union introduced the AI Act, the world’s first comprehensive AI law, which categorizes AI systems according to their risk (minimal, limited, high, and unacceptable).wikipedia+1​\\n\\n\\nHigh-risk applications are subject to strict requirements, while systems with unacceptable risk, such as government-run social scoring, are banned altogether.artificialintelligenceact​\\n\\n\\nThe AI Act emphasizes human oversight, transparency, and non-discrimination, with a compliance timeline and provisions for innovation.europarl.europa+1​\\n\\n\\nOther countries, like Brazil, have adopted legal AI frameworks inspired by the EU’s approach.artificialintelligenceact​\\n\\nUnited States Regulation\\n\\nThere is currently no comprehensive federal law dedicated solely to regulating AI in the U.S..whitecase+1​\\n\\n\\nU.S. regulation relies on existing privacy, consumer protection, and sector-specific laws, with federal authorities clarifying that these laws apply to AI-enabled systems.whitecase​\\n\\n\\nRecent state-level laws, such as California’s Transparency in Frontier Artificial Intelligence Act, have introduced requirements for transparency, safety, and incident reporting, focusing on “trust but verify” oversight rather than outright bans.rstreet​\",\"citations\":[\"https://www.rstreet.org/commentary/california-regulation-frenzy-risks-burgeoning-ai-industry/\",\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regulation_of_artificial_intelligence\",\"https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/\",\"https://www.europarl.europa.eu/topics/en/article/20230601STO93804/eu-ai-act-first-regulation-on-artificial-intelligence\",\"https://www.whitecase.com/insight-our-thinking/ai-watch-global-regulatory-tracker-united-states\"],\"extractionConfidence\":1,\"extractionWarnings\":[]}"
